{"name":"Pearl Bush","hex":"#ded1c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pearl bush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Exochorda."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pearl_bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Exochorda","blocks":[{"text":"Exochorda is a small genus of flowering plants in the family Rosaceae, native to China and central Asia (Turkestan). They are used as ornamental plants with the common name pearl bush, or pearlbush. Numerous species have been described on the basis of differing appearance and geographical separation, but a systematic study revealed that the different types are closely related and probably all descended from a single species that formerly had a wide distribution that has been fragmented by habitat loss. As a single species the correct name is E. racemosa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Exochorda_korolkowii_-_Botanical_Garden_in_Kaisaniemi%2C_Helsinki_-_DSC03604.JPG/330px-Exochorda_korolkowii_-_Botanical_Garden_in_Kaisaniemi%2C_Helsinki_-_DSC03604.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exochorda","wikidata":"Q137339"},{"title":"Pearl","blocks":[{"text":"A pearl is a hard, shiny object produced within the soft tissue of a living shelled mollusk. Like the shell of a mollusk, a pearl is composed of calcium carbonate in a crystalline form, which is deposited in concentric layers. More commercially valuable pearls are perfectly round and smooth, but many other shapes, known as baroque pearls, can occur. The highest quality of natural pearls have been highly valued as gemstones and objects of beauty for many centuries. In literature, pearls have become a metaphor for something rare, fine, admirable, and valuable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Various_pearls.jpg/330px-Various_pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl","wikidata":"Q43436"},{"title":"Pearl (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color pearl is a pale tint of off-white. It is a representation of the average color of a pearl."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/PerlmuttAusst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl_(color)","wikidata":"Q7158021"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg/120px-Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg/250px-Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg/120px-Pearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearlbush_Exochorda_racemosa_Leaf_Stalk_2000px.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg/250px-Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg/500px-Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg/250px-Exochorda_x_macrantha_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki